'''Anna Cazenave Cambet''' is a French film director born on 13 August 1990, in [[Nérac]].

== Career ==

After completing her photography studies at ETPA Toulouse, Anna Cazenave Cambert joined [[La Fémis]] (department of "Directing") from which she graduated in 2017.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Anna Cazenave Cambet|url=https://www.semainedelacritique.com/fr/realisateurs/cazenave-cambet-anna|website=Semaine de la Critique du Festival de Cannes|access-date=2025-11-30|language=fr}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=LOVE ME TENDER – The American French Film Festival in Los Angeles |url=https://theamericanfrenchfilmfestival.org/love-me-tender/ |access-date=2026-08-06 |language=en-US}}</ref>

Her debut feature film, ''De l'or pour les chiens'', released in 2020, was presented at the [[2021 Cannes Film Festival]] as part of the [[Critics' Week]] selection.<ref>Gisèle Breteau Skira, ''[[:fr:Jeune Cinéma|Jeune Cinéma]]'', {{numéro|408–409}}, summer 2021</ref> She received the Youth Prize for ''Love Me Tender'' at the 39th [[Cabourg Film Festival]].

