'''Takafumi Uchimoto''' ({{langx|ja|内本 隆文}}, born 19 February 1998) is a Japanese [[soft tennis]] player. A right-handed back player, he represents [[Japan]] internationally and plays for NTT West. He is a two-time Asian champion in men's singles and men's doubles, having won the singles title at the 2016 Asian Soft Tennis Championships and the doubles title at the 2025 Asian Soft Tennis Championships. He has also won gold medals in the men's team event at the [[2022 Asian Games]] and [[2026 Asian Games]].<ref name="JOC">{{cite web |title=内本 隆文 |url=https://www.joc.or.jp/athletes/uchimototakafumi/index.html |access-date=3 October 2026 |publisher=[[Japanese Olympic Committee]]}}</ref>

== Career ==
Uchimoto was born on 19 February 1998 in [[Osaka Prefecture]]. He began playing soft tennis at the age of six after being introduced to the sport by his parents. He attended Uemiya Junior High School and Uemiya High School before studying at [[Waseda University]]. He joined NTT West after graduating from university.<ref name="ASTAF">{{cite web |title=UCHIMOTO Takafumi |url=https://www.ocagames.com/HZ_Info/AG2022-/en/results/soft-tennis/athlete-profile-n2014615-uchimoto-takafumi.htm |access-date=3 October 2026 |publisher=Hangzhou Asian Games Organising Committee}}</ref>

Uchimoto won multiple national titles during his junior and university career, including the All Japan Intercollegiate team championship in 2016 and 2017. He also won the men's singles and doubles events at the 2015 Inter-High School Championships, partnering with Kaito Maruyama in the doubles event.<ref name="STM">{{cite web |title=内本 隆文 |url=https://www.softtennis-mag.com/players/%E5%86%85%E6%9C%AC-%E9%9A%86%E6%96%87%EF%BC%88%E3%81%86%E3%81%A1%E3%82%82%E3%81%A8%E3%83%BB%E3%81%9F%E3%81%8B%E3%81%B5%E3%81%BF%EF%BC%89/ |access-date=3 October 2026 |publisher=Soft Tennis Magazine}}</ref>

In 2016, Uchimoto made his senior international debut at the 2016 Asian Soft Tennis Championships in Chiba, Japan. He won the men's singles gold medal and the men's doubles silver medal with Kaito Maruyama.<ref name="ASTAF" /><ref name="STM" />

At the 2019 World Soft Tennis Championships in Taizhou, China, Uchimoto won the men's team gold medal and the mixed doubles bronze medal with Rurika Kuroki.<ref name="ASTAF" />

Uchimoto represented Japan at the [[2022 Asian Games]], held in Hangzhou in 2023. He won the men's team gold medal as part of the Japanese team alongside Hayato Funemizu, Sora Hirooka, Riku Uchida and Toshiki Uematsu.<ref name="AsianGames">{{cite web |title=Soft Tennis UCHIMOTO Takafumi |url=https://www.ocagames.com/HZ_Info/AG2022-/en/results/soft-tennis/athlete-profile-n2014615-uchimoto-takafumi.htm |access-date=3 October 2026 |publisher=Hangzhou Asian Games Organising Committee}}</ref>

In 2025, Uchimoto returned to the Japanese national team for the 2025 Asian Soft Tennis Championships in Mungyeong, South Korea. He won the men's doubles title with Toshiki Uematsu, defeating fellow Japanese pair Shunsuke Ueoka and Kaito Maruyama in the final. Japan also won the men's team event.<ref name="YONEX">{{cite web |title=7種目中6種目制覇・日本代表がアジアを席巻！！ 第9回 アジアソフトテニス選手権 |url=https://www.yonex.co.jp/news/2025/3419.html |access-date=3 October 2026 |publisher=[[Yonex]]}}</ref>

In June 2026, Uchimoto and Rena Yoshida finished runners-up at the All Japan Mixed Doubles Soft Tennis Championships, losing to Rena Temma and Takuya Kurosaka in the final.<ref name="YONEX2026">{{cite web |date=10 June 2026 |title=天間麗奈・黒坂卓矢ペアが初優勝！天間は連覇達成！第7回全日本ミックスダブルス選手権大会 |url=https://www.yonex.co.jp/news/2026/3926.html |access-date=3 October 2026 |publisher=[[Yonex]]}}</ref>

At the [[2026 Asian Games]] in Aichi-Nagoya, Uchimoto won his second consecutive Asian Games men's team gold medal as a member of the Japanese team.<ref name="JOC" />

